<section class="section" id="editor">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2><span class="hash">##</span>The markdown is the document</h2>
    <p>
      There is no preview pane and no mode to switch into. A heading is heading-sized while
      you type it. The <code>#</code> that makes it one stays in the file and fades back
      until your cursor lands on that line, so what you see is always what is on disk.
    </p>
    <p>
      Bullets and checkboxes go one step further: Milky draws them over the plain
      <code>-</code> and <code>[x]</code> characters rather than replacing them. The page
      reads like Notes; the file stays plain text that anyone — or any other program — can
      open.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
